{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfDwEjxE8uHb4KTzMnuTm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`go vet ./...` and `go test -race ./...` pass with no failures; the working tree is clean with four commits on `hive/SCRUM-7`.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Ticket lifecycle logging** (`internal/dispatch/handle.go`, `dispatch.go`)\n- `picked up ticket` — logged right after the claim is won, with the ticket key and summary.\n- `work started` — logged when the executor is invoked, with `attempt=n/max` and whether it's a resume.\n- One closing line per outcome, each carrying `result=<what the ticket was told>`:\n  - `work finished` (completed; includes `pr=<url>` or `branch=`)\n  - `work needs info` (triage question or executor `HIVE_NEEDS_INPUT` question)\n  - `work needs human` (triage reject, or attempts exhausted — includes `cause`)\n  - `work failed` (retryable failure — includes `cause` and `attempt`)\n- Removed the per-poll `handled ticket=… outcome=skipped` info line, which was effectively polling noise. The error path in `Once` is unchanged.\n- New `Dispatcher.Polled func(time.Time)` hook, fired after each successful poll (not when the run window is closed).\n\n**Live \"last poll\" status line** (`internal/statusline`, `cmd/hivedispatch/main.go`)\n- New stdlib-only `statusline.Line`: `Set` rewrites one terminal line in place; it also implements `io.Writer` so the slog handler writes *through* it — each log line erases the status, prints, and redraws, so the two never interleave.\n- `run` shows `last poll 2026-09-20 02:42:15 (12s ago)`, refreshed every second, only when stderr is a TTY and not `-once`. Pipes/files get plain logs. The line is erased on shutdown.\n\n**Tests**: dispatcher tests now capture log output and assert each lifecycle line; `Polled` hook tests; `statusline` byte-sequence and concurrency tests; `pollStatus` formatting and `showLastPoll` wiring tests in `cmd`.\n\n**Docs**: decision recorded in `docs/decisions.md` (why polling is shown on a status line rather than logged; TUI/third-party lib rejected).\n\nOne caveat: I couldn't run a live pseudo-terminal smoke test (the `script` command was denied), so the TTY rendering is verified by unit tests on the exact escape bytes rather than by eye. Worth a quick look on the next real `hivedispatch run`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":259,"cache_read_input_tokens":91496,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":259},"output_tokens":783,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d03743be-102a-4205-897d-42c84124a341","uuid":"5bf36cc8-01f5-4340-9614-1982e9944e07","timestamp":"2026-09-20T02:54:02.563Z","request_id":"req_011CfDwEj4e4sWnujPUx7Qzf"}
